<title>USA: CME May lumber limit up on strong bonds, stocks.</title>
<headline>CME May lumber limit up on strong bonds, stocks.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>CME May lumber futures were up the $10.00 per thousand board foot limit at midmorning, boosted by spillover strength from surging bond and stock markets, floor sources said.</p>
<p>May was bid up the $10.00 limit at $404.60. July was also sharply higher, after briefly touching the $10.00 per tbf limit, and at 1043 CDT stood $9.20 higher at $402.50.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
